{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1725 (IDE adopts the eDE shell): what the IDE's sidebar shows, a pure projection of the host's state, replayed in TS (src/ide.ts) and Rust (uicore-model ide.rs). The document apps/ede/ui/sidebar.json binds the result under /shell/ide; eDE never feeds that path. The nav's order is Needs you (while any, or on its page), Chats, Devices, Drafts (while any, or on its page): the IDE has no start menu (#EXP-1741), so Devices is a nav row; the person's Assistant is the sidebar's corner. screen = the open screen as <kind> or <kind>:<id>. A row's selected follows screen; an active row is lit on its root and on any session of its tree; an app row on its id or its slug. An agent's dot = amber (needs you) before green (busy). gear = the row's hover gear: agents and apps for every member, boards for owners; agents.add = the owner's new agent button. boards.empty = the team has no boards, the list's empty state. Pinned and Active hide while empty: the document reads their length. base holds the input every case starts from; a case overrides keys of it. copy = the nav's words (chat-list.json copy.title and needs-you.json copy.entry). tabs: the bottom tab bar (#EXP-1726, docs/tabbar.json): every open tab in tab order, work tabs and terminals merged, activeTab = the active key while a tab holds the screen.",
